  "body": "## Scoped research result (2026-10-16 KST)\nStacked **DRAFT** on PR #154 exact `daf653e87a5b208ed6f51113e83d56fec4abf4f8`. Original photon `source_aware.py` is byte-identical (Git blob `db822a53da3ccdca7cf96628e9ef3bbcec83db5a`); no production PR150 source, checkpoints, active NCP work or other branch is modified.\n\n- New **frozen-rate manufactured** reversible-H/He comparator: exact positive collisional ionization logistic subflow, original exact RR pair, symmetric Strang composition with source-locked three-species Verner photon photoionization, and proper per-H thermal/binding/bolometric escape ledgers.\n- The electron fraction is derived from HII + HeII + 2HeIII; collisional electron production, recombination electron loss, nuclei and photon event counts tracked; rejected inadequate thermal budget, no spurious clipping.\n- Added strictly read-only `native_photo_contract.py` mapping photon nodes to actual PR150 `IgmPhotoInput` with `gamma_s` and `heat_erg_per_absorber_s`. The original native `igm_point_rhs` must remain the sole owner of **physical** CI/RR/DR/CE/freefree/CMB and photo consumption. This PR is *not* an auto-merge or native chemistry replacement.\n- Source-native snapshot: PR150 at `fe789b0b13b1883c5a74cbc907f72f6f963a5d66` with exact Git blob IDs in `contracts/native_authority.json`; snapshot must be rebound to newest HEAD before code mutation.\n\n## Actual local execution\n- **29/29 new Python test PASS** and **22/22 original PR154 tests rerun PASS**, Git blob identity checked.\n- Independent full unsplit SciPy DOP853 controlled manufactured-rate ODE, measured error order **1.9993293411871906** on last five refinements; at 256 substeps max state discrepancy **5.899466941628e-7**, absolute energy ledger residual **2.56e-13 eV/H**.\n- Local 32-case science JSON from 1 vs 2 processes byte identical, no NCP scaling claim.\n- Wolfram Language direct algebraic CI ODE, IC, stiff limit and photo/CI/RR energy identity residuals **{0,0,0,0}**.\n- Reproducible portable archive including full logs/plots/code/tests/README/WL/native contract/NCP instructions and `codex_handoff_prompt.md`. `./verify.sh` passed after **fresh independent ZIP extraction** (51 tests).\n\n## Strict claim status\n**Manufactured coefficients** are not physical Grackle rates. Bolometric RR escrow lacks an emitted spectrum and is not reinjected into UV photons. No physical thermal (Case-A) RR/CI calibration, DR/CE/freefree/CMB, T-dependent rate feedback, recombination source age, baryon Euler recoil, native Rust parity, full z20\u21924 EoR solution, observational result or NCP execution is claimed.\n\n**Remote blocker:** Desktop Commander monthly quota exhausted; connected Ubuntu/NCP cannot be controlled in this turn. Precise read-first Codex and NCP guide are included for user-authorized execution after control is available.\n\nDo not merge into PR150 automatically. Native source owner parity and full physical ledger reconciliation are the next gate.",
